in: f64:0xC33EB208C2DC0000
out: value: f64:0xC33EB208C2DC0000
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: Date.parse reads back none of this engine's own toUTCString renderings for a year below 1 or above 9999 and answers NaN, where it must answer the time value rendered (21.4.3.2): the .NET formats it parses with cannot hold the year. Answered by Broiler.JS docs/roadmap/SharedLibraries.md, SJL-6.5 (the Date area's record; the correspondence's row P9).
divergence.broiler-vm: Date.parse reads back none of this engine's own toUTCString renderings for a negative year and answers NaN, where it must answer the time value rendered (21.4.3.2): its textual reader takes no sign on the year. Answered by Broiler.VM docs/javascript-shared-libraries/milestones/sjl-6-date.md, SJL-6.4 (JSD-0072; the correspondence's row P9).
