out: value: f64:0xC2CC4189166C0000
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: The instant 0001-01-01T00:00:00.000Z is this engine's invalid-date sentinel, so a date at that instant, whether a setter or the constructor makes it, is invalid: the setter answers NaN, and toUTCString answers Invalid Date, which Date.parse reads as NaN, where the time value is -62135596800000. Answered by Broiler.JS docs/roadmap/SharedLibraries.md, SJL-6.5 (the Date area's record; the correspondence's row D3).
